R-PB10 R-PB8 R-SM2 R-SM4 R-J6 R-OUT4 (slice 218b, Design Q598): the platform `acme/pfq` 0.6.0 has 2 targets (x64musl, arm64musl) and a `requires` clause with 2 entries, so R-SM2 gives no smoke app (`Smoke.app_text` is `NoSmoke`). The platform is in `packages/`, the world is that of `sm1`.
Run 1 (`--json`): no build. The only `random` is the one of the fetch step (`Fetch.packages!`: the dir is there, no download); there is no `make_dirs`, no `write_atomic` of a smoke app, no `probes` and no `db_write`, so no temp dir and no row in `smoke`. `data.smoke` has each target of the header with the result `no-smoke-app`, the exit is 0, the text is on stderr (R-OUT4). Run 2 (`--target arm64musl`, no `--json`): the same for the one target, in the text.
